{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Different Shades Of Blue feels like a natural next choice because I want more expressive blues guitar after Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "A Fool To Care connects directly with my interest in Memphis: another Boz Scaggs album offers the soulful blues singing I want to hear again."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Purple Album's heavier hard rock and The Endless River's atmospheric instrumentals miss the blues songs and vocals I feel like hearing now.",
    "Nothing Has Changed and 25 offer less of the guitar-led blues and roots sound that makes me interested enough to choose an album today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Interest in Clapton and Hendrix seems to have been stretched into a broad interest in famous rock artists, even though their blues connection matters more to me right now.",
    "Familiar names and older material seem to count too much: a deluxe Zeppelin release or archival Beatles performances are less urgent to me than another album that fits my current listening mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of soulful vocals and blues guitar matters more to my choices than simply sharing a rock audience with albums I have heard.",
    "An appealing connection is not always enough for me to act: Hypnotic Eye's link to Benmont Tench and Nathaniel Rateliff's rootsy soul interest me, but familiar blues artists take priority today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in blues and roots music but stretched it too broadly into rock familiarity instead of focusing on what I would choose now."
}"}
